# CC-Track logging (paste into your project's CLAUDE.md)

This project is tracked by CC-Track. Whenever you start a non-trivial piece of work:

1. Create a plan: `cctrack plan add --title "<short imperative title>"` — note the printed plan id.
2. Break the work into tasks: `cctrack task add --plan <plan-id> --content "<task>"` for each step. Add `--desc "<detail>"` when a task needs more than its short name.
3. As you work, keep statuses current:
   - starting a task: `cctrack task start <task-id>`
   - finishing a task: `cctrack task done <task-id>`
4. When the work is finished: `cctrack plan done <plan-id>`.

Rules:
- Don't create plans for one-line questions or trivial edits.
- The `cctrack` CLI targets the current session automatically (hooks keep it in sync).
- Never block on cctrack failures — if it errors, just continue with the actual work.
